    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two independent failure origins converge on the same downstream failure mode (fm_uvtrip): the legacy drawing/mis-assignment chain (root cause, code B) and the physically separate breaker micrologic trip-device defect (proximate hardware failure causing MCC deenergization). Both are necessary conditions for the unexpected trip path per the narrative ('breaker failure caused two of the four undervoltage relays...to deenergize...creating an unexpected trip path'), so fm_bkrfail/fm_mccdeenerg and fm_misassign both LEADS_TO fm_uvtrip. Only fm_drawing (origin of the officially coded root cause) has a CAUSED_BY edge to the Cause node per rule 5. 2A MFW pump trip on low flow (due to manually isolated recirc valve) and 2B MFRV seat leakage are described as contributing to the safety-significance discussion of AFAS timing, but are secondary design-context/analysis details, not part of the main causal chain to the trip itself; modeled as components only, not chained. Auxiliary feedwater (BA) is modeled as an actuated system per event description, not as a stated BACKED_UP_BY target since it itself actuated (is part of the consequence chain), whereas main feedwater (SJ) explicitly 'was always immediately available throughout this event' -> backup edge."
}